=== PARITY (vs web RequestBuilder.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; it is a controlled form driven by
    props (`endpoint`, `onSend`, `loading`) with NO data hook / NO network of its own (the actual HTTP
    is the parent's `onSend`). The native parity binds through a local P1/S8 state holder
    (RequestBuilderModel) that owns the editable request state the web `useState`/`useEffect` hooks hold
    and hands a `SendRequest` to the host on send. The view performs no HTTP — there is none to perform.
  buildUrl -> RequestBuilderAdapter.relativeURL is a faithful port: `{name}` path substitution (empty
    value keeps the `{name}` token, first-occurrence replace like JS String.replace), `&`-joined query
    of the params that carry a value, each value `encodeURIComponent`-encoded (unreserved + !~*'() left
    raw; verified `a b`->`a%20b`, `/?=&`->`%2F%3F%3D%26`). `displayURL` prefixes `/api/v1` (URL bar)
    while `relativeURL` is what `onSend` receives — matching the web `/api/v1{buildUrl()}` display vs
    `onSend(buildUrl(), …)`. All verified by EXECUTED XCTest.
  body seed / JSON -> RequestJSONFormatter reproduces `JSON.stringify(example, null, 2)` exactly
    (two-space indent, ordered object members via an ordered RequestJSON tree, `,\n` separators, empty
    `{}`/`[]` collapse, JSON string + C0-control escaping, integers without a `.0` tail). seedBody
    returns the pretty example, the `"{\n  \n}"` skeleton when a body is required without an example,
    or "" when there is no body — the web body effect. EXECUTED-green (nested object/array, escaping,
    empty collapse, scalar vectors).
  destructive confirm -> the web `isDestructive = method !== 'GET'` two-step send is ported: the first
    `send()` on a non-GET opens the amber confirm row (no onSend), the next `send()` (or any GET) builds
    the headers + `SendRequest` and hands it to the host; `cancel()` dismisses. `body || undefined` ->
    `body.isEmpty ? nil`. A trimmed non-empty API key becomes `X-API-Key`. EXECUTED-green.
  composition -> URL bar (web MethodBadge colored mono chip -> token-tinted RequestMethodBadge + the
    scrollable `/api/v1…` code + the Send control whose label flips to "Sending…" and disables while
    `loading`) · destructive confirm banner · summary + (distinct) description · Path Parameters panel ·
    Query Parameters panel · Request Body panel (+ content-type accessory) · Authentication (Optional)
    panel (always shown) — each panel is the web `GlassPanel` mapped to the shared `.tsGlassPanel()`
    material with an uppercase muted header.
  shared components -> reuses the shared TSButton (Components/UI/Buttons) for Send / Yes,send / Cancel,
    and the shared `.tsGlassPanel()` material (Design/TSMaterial) for the web `GlassPanel` sections,
    compiled against the REAL sources in the typechecks below. The inputs (web `Input`/`Textarea`) are
    composed from SwiftUI `TextField`/`SecureField`/`TextEditor` + a token field-chrome modifier so the
    field prompts can resolve through this surface's P1/S10 table (the shared `TSTextField` takes only a
    LocalizedStringKey prompt against the main catalog). Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map).
  States (all render) -> the web source's branches are reproduced, each with a #if DEBUG preview:
      • loading  -> the Send control shows "Sending…" + disables (web `loading ? t('playground.sending')`).
      • confirm  -> the destructive confirm banner (web `confirmOpen`).
      • content  -> the path / query / body sections render only when present (web conditional panels).
      • empty    -> an endpoint with no params + no body shows only the URL bar + the always-present
                    auth panel (web behavior) — never a blank box.
